{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Calibration grid",
  "_about": "Calibration: lines every 50 px with x/y labels, a grey swatch drawn by a shader and the same one as pixels, a probe row L1..L16 of own image layers, and an atlas-text probe. The app's own connection carries the grid, the labels, the two swatches, L1..L3 and the atlas text (8 layers); L4..L8 are on connection 2, L9..L12 on 3 and L13..L16 on 4. A photo showing all sixteen means each socket gets its own 8 layers. The atlas text (ATLAS, the clock, the rpm) is one shader layer reading an R8 glyph asset: if it shows, text can be drawn with no pixel writes at all.",
